  "method_notes": [
    "20 synthetic weekdays, not an exchange holiday calendar; 64 codes, alternating 1m/3m, quote ratio + fill strength + 10-level depth, one chart fitted to requested history.",
    "Each configuration uses a fresh browser context. Initial chart mount precedes the cold stage; the first revisit repeats the current code. Two runs reverse configuration order. Each visit waits for the expected candle and both indicator histories, then two animation frames.",
    "Times are observed development-build results with fixed 35ms mock API delay; no vendor network/WS load, low-memory device test, cache-expiry revisit, or multi-hour soak. Each context revisits before the 30min raw-range GC.",
    "Heap is renderer JS heap only. Peak is the largest per-visit sample, not a continuous maximum. Retained heap is sampled after explicit GC outside timings. Raw and canonical estimates share objects and must not be added.",
    "Pointer metric means pointer event to next animation frame, not full end-to-end tooltip paint. Cold-stage pointer samples are absent; raw output uses zero, summary uses null.",
    "GC numbers are trace-event durations (MajorGC/MinorGC), not a guaranteed stop-the-world pause measurement. Runtime test assertions check chart completion and unhandled JS exceptions; console warnings are recorded, not a passing performance budget.",
    "fixtureSha256 hashes seed parameters only; the generator and executable sources are covered by inputs.json.gz."
  ],
